// ---- App library engine (docs/07-app-library.md) ---------------------------
// Bump when the vupp.* Lua surface changes incompatibly; manifests declare
// min_engine and the catalog/device refuse apps that need a newer engine.
// v2: real gfx.sprite/gfx.image (.vsp assets), palettes up to 255 colors,
//     vupp.sfx WAV samples, tone waveforms — v1 apps run unchanged.
// v3: gfx.texcol/vline/shademap — the C textured-column fast path for
//     raycaster-style apps (Lua casts the rays, C pushes the pixels).
// v4: gfx.tload/terrain/theight/ssprite — heightfield terrain renderer with a
//     per-pixel depth buffer plus a scaled (optionally depth-tested) sprite
//     blit, for open-world third-person apps (Lua drives the camera and
//     billboards, C marches the terrain and pushes the pixels).
// v5: gfx.tri — flat-shaded triangle rasterizer, for low-poly 3D apps
//     (Lua transforms/sorts the faces painter-style, C fills the spans).
// v6: gfx.floor — per-scanline affine textured ground plane (Mode 7 style)
//     sampling the loaded terrain colormap, for top-down driving apps
//     (Lua drives the camera and sprites, C sweeps the scanlines).
// v7: engine-level START pause menu (resume / restart / exit) replaces the
//     per-app hold-B-to-quit convention — START never reaches apps, B belongs
//     to gameplay; optional vupp.on_exit() runs at teardown for exit-time
//     saves/emits; palette indices 253/254 are engine-reserved white/black.
// v8: gfx.text draws each size from its own glyph set (4x6 / 8x12 / 12x18)
//     instead of upscaling the 4x6 one, and size 3 is no longer clamped to 2 —
//     legible letterforms for early readers. Metrics are unchanged (advance
//     4*size, line height 6*size), so v7 layouts render identically; only apps
//     whose layout needs true size 3 have to declare min_engine 8.
// v9: NO Lua surface change. This one marks firmware that can install a
//     PRIVATE package — a family-authored app from the family-apps bucket,
//     fetched with the device JWT and verified against its sha256 — where
//     everything before it hardcodes an anonymous GET of the public
//     app-library bucket and would fail-loop on one.
//
//     That deliberately overloads what "engine version" means: this is an
//     install-capability flag wearing a Lua-API version's clothes. It is the
//     only gate that works RETROACTIVELY, which is the whole reason — an
//     already-shipped device cannot be taught a new field, but it already
//     refuses anything whose min_engine it does not recognise, and the Apps
//     tab already renders that refusal as "needs a device update". A second,
//     honest capability flag would do nothing for the devices that are
//     already out there. See docs/17-studio.md "Distribution".
export const APP_ENGINE_VERSION = 9
export const APP_CANVAS_W = 160 // portrait canvas, integer-scaled 2x to the panel
export const APP_CANVAS_H = 240
export const APP_FPS_DEFAULT = 30
// Indexed color: manifests may declare up to 255 palette entries; index 255 is
